        "answer": {
          "short": "$3024$.\n\nChoose the five odd-digit positions, then arrange the four even digits.",
          "worked": "Choose five of the nine positions for $1,3,5,7,9$. Their increasing order fixes their placement. The four even digits can occupy the remaining positions in $4!$ orders.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=\\binom{9}{5}\\times4!\\\\N&=126\\times24\\\\N&=3024.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
