        "answer": {
          "short": "$126$.\n\nChoosing the odd-digit positions fixes both digit orders.",
          "worked": "Choose five of the nine positions for the odd digits. Put $1,3,5,7,9$ into those positions in increasing order and $2,4,6,8$ into the remaining positions in increasing order. Each choice gives exactly one arrangement.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=\\binom{9}{5}\\\\N&=126.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      }
